---
description: BeanBox fix — copy the repro test into the PR and make that same test pass
alwaysApply: true
---

Make the smallest change that fixes the root cause of the GitHub issue.

- The issue lists a reproduction test (`beanbox-repro`). Copy that file from the triage branch into this PR.
- Make that same test pass.
- Never skip or weaken it. Do not use `.skip` or `.todo`, and do not delete or loosen its assertions.
- Do not edit `tests/repro` beyond that copy. That file was named before the GitHub issue existed.
- When the task states `Issue #<n>` and the machine token `issue-<n>`, the pull request title starts with `Issue #<n>:` and the branch name contains `issue-<n>`. The issue URL and `Fixes #<n>` stay in the body. A case id in the task is a secondary reference, not a substitute for the issue number.

Run `npm test`. `tests/cart.test.ts` and `tests/images.test.ts` must pass. `productImageUrl` for a bean id must return the path that exists under `public/` (bean files are in `public/images/beans/`).

Hard bans:

- The copied repro test must be byte-identical. If the test is truly wrong, stop and report instead of editing it.
- No `.skip`, `.only`, `.todo`, `try/catch` around asserts, loosened matchers, or longer timeouts.
- No new mocks of the code under fix.
- No edits to test config, CI or workflow files, package scripts, or snapshots.
- Never weaken validation, auth, the signed confirm, or user scoping.

## PR description requirements

Every fix PR description must begin with these three lines, replacing all placeholders with facts from this run:

Root cause: <explain the defect and why it caused the reported behaviour>
Files changed: <list changed file paths and briefly explain each change>
Proof: <name the original repro test, the command run, and its result>

Do not claim a test passed unless you ran it and observed it passing.
If verification could not complete, state that explicitly in Proof.

These reporting requirements do not replace or relax any existing
repro-test preservation, minimal-fix, security, or verification rules